<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea-Mobil consortium finds gas off Vietnam.</title>
<headline>S.Korea-Mobil consortium finds gas off Vietnam.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>A consortium of South Korean companies, including state-run Korea Petroleum Development Corp (PEDCO), and Mobil Corp has found natural gas and condensate off Vietnam, a PEDCO spokesman said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>The find amounts to 33 million cubic feet per day of natural gas and 963 barrels per day of condensate at a well in offshore Block 11-2 east of Vietnam, the PEDCO spokesman said.</p>
<p>A group of eight Korean firms holds a 55 percent stake in the venture. The Korean consortium signed a production sharing contract with the Vietnamese government in May 1992 and Mobil joined the group in March this year, he said.</p>
<p>The eight Korean firms are PEDCO, Daewoo Corp, Hyundai Corp, Daesung Industries, LG International Corp, Ssangyong Corp, Samsung Corp and Sam Whan Corp.</p>
